steps.explanation:
\[
v_{Vol}(t)=\frac1V\frac{dx(t)}{dt}
\]

بما أن:
\[
x(t)=\frac{V_{H_2}(t)}{V_M}
\]
فإن:
\[
\frac{dx(t)}{dt}
=\frac1{V_M}\frac{dV_{H_2}(t)}{dt}
\]
إذن:
\[
\boxed{
v_{Vol}(t)
=\frac1{V\,V_M}
\frac{dV_{H_2}(t)}{dt}
}
\]

مع:
\[
V=100mL=0.100L,\qquad V_M=24L\cdot mol^{-1}
\]
نجد:
\[
v_{Vol}(0)
=\frac{0.021}{0.100\times24}
=8.75\times10^{-3}
mol\cdot L^{-1}\cdot min^{-1}
\]
أي:
\[
\boxed{
v_{Vol}(0)\approx8.7\times10^{-3}
mol\cdot L^{-1}\cdot min^{-1}
}
\]
